            <ArticleTitle>Laminin associated with BMP7 as potential secondary astrocytic glioma fiber differentiation targets.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3611-3616</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">12054</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To investigate the activation of the BMP7 and laminin pathway is associated with glioma cell proliferation and differentiation.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="PATIENTS AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">We enrolled 65 patients with primary operable glioma. Laminin and BMP7 protein expression and its subcellular localization were studied by immunofluorescence.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">We detected a higher level of BMP7 expression in glioma tissue in patients with a lower grade of glioma who had a lower eosinophil count. Compared to patients with a higher grade of glioma, we observed a lower level of laminin expression in patients with a lower grade of glioma.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Our data indicated a potential link between eosinophil counts and the expression levels of laminin and BMP7 in glioma differentiation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
